{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CCvx1HmtoDSpeZovYvEMzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity-and-R&D control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Grounded summary of what it is:\n\n**Purpose**\n- A single-folder, plain-markdown productivity system (tasks, projects, inbox, weekly reviews) with no database, no syncing, and no external dependencies â€” Python stdlib only (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n- Markdown files are the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.); everything else reads/writes those.\n\n**What it does (productivity core)**\n- Ships `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes changes back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service **`anchor`** (you don't launch it by hand).\n- Ships `anchor.py` â€” a CLI mirror of the same logic that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n- Manages a task lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) across domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n- Runs a daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, walks a synthetic task through all states, and writes dated health reports.\n\n**What it ships (R&D \"Project Cockpit\" surface)**\n- A per-project R&D control surface that turns Anchor into \"mission control\" for trio-driven work (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman), built up over four design generations (v1â€“v4), all merged to master. v4 \"Project Cockpit\" is the current state (merge `38fd70e`, 9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passed).\n- It models project work as **sessions** (one trio run = one session), with cached/validated AI-generated summaries, a 5-lane Kanban (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass Catchers), and a project cost/tokens/time rollup.\n- Real interactive **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket / SSE transport), each isolated in its own git worktree, where a new session auto-loads the lane's skill once and greets once. Supports an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only).\n- Deliverable launch-by-type (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port hard-guarded â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render), stage handoffs between planâ†’build, and Ghost World Labs branding (\"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\").\n\nIn short: **a stdlib-only, markdown-backed local productivity dashboard for one user, extended into a durable, terminal-driven control surface for running and remembering AI \"trio\" R&D projects.**\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from `CLAUDE.md` and the locked design docs, not from re-reading the source this session â€” I can verify any specific claim against the actual modules if you want."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd235878-0fd2-49b4-95a0-2b63deca59a2","uuid":"2384374a-d422-4b64-b8e6-b64a3fad66c7","request_id":"req_011Cc1JDeQ4HnZpovoHbxyty"}
